# Architecture Rules — Project Equinox

## The Canonical Market Model
This is the single most important struct in the system.
Everything flows through it. Never bypass it.

```go
// models/market.go — the one true market representation
type Market struct {
    // Identity
    ID         string    // internal UUID (generated by us, not the venue)
    VenueID    string    // the ID the venue uses natively
    Venue      string    // "kalshi" or "polymarket" — always lowercase
    Title      string    // normalized question text (lowercase, no punctuation)

    // Pricing — all three stored explicitly
    YesBid     float64   // highest price someone will buy Yes (0.0 to 1.0)
    YesAsk     float64   // lowest price someone will sell Yes (0.0 to 1.0)
    YesMid     float64   // (YesBid + YesAsk) / 2 — midpoint price
    NoPrice    float64   // 1.0 - YesMid — always derived, never stored separately
    Spread     float64   // YesAsk - YesBid — tighter = healthier market

    // Liquidity
    Liquidity  float64   // total $ available in order book
    Volume24h  float64   // trading volume in last 24 hours

    // Timing
    ResolvesAt time.Time // when the market closes and resolves
    FetchedAt  time.Time // when we pulled this data (staleness detection)

    // Metadata
    Category   string    // "politics", "economics", "crypto", "sports", "other"
    Status     string    // "open", "closed", "resolved"

    // Debug — always preserve original API response
    RawData    interface{} // original API response, never modified
}
```

## Supporting Models

```go
// models/market.go continued

// MatchResult — output of equivalence detection
type MatchResult struct {
    MarketA     Market
    MarketB     Market
    IsMatch     bool
    AreOpposites bool    // true if they are mirror images of the same event
    Confidence  float64
    Method      string   // "heuristic", "ai", "heuristic+ai"
    Reasoning   string
    Warnings    []string
    MatchedAt   time.Time
}

// VenueScore — routing engine score for one venue
type VenueScore struct {
    Venue          string
    PriceScore     float64  // 0.0 to 1.0 — higher = better price
    SpreadScore    float64  // 0.0 to 1.0 — higher = tighter spread
    LiquidityScore float64  // 0.0 to 1.0 — higher = deeper book
    TotalScore     float64  // weighted combination
}

// RoutingDecision — output of routing engine
type RoutingDecision struct {
    Market           Market
    OrderSide        string    // "yes" or "no"
    OrderSize        float64   // hypothetical $ amount
    RecommendedVenue string    // "kalshi" or "polymarket"
    Confidence       float64   // how clear-cut the decision was
    VenueScores      []VenueScore
    Reasoning        string    // human-readable explanation
    Warnings         []string  // caveats, stale data, missing info
    DecidedAt        time.Time
}
```

