## Routing Weight Constants
These weights are design decisions. Document them.

```go
// routing/engine.go
const (
    // PriceWeight is highest because it directly affects P&L
    PriceWeight = 0.40

    // LiquidityWeight is second because order fill depends on it
    LiquidityWeight = 0.35

    // SpreadWeight is third as a market health indicator
    SpreadWeight = 0.25
)
// Invariant: PriceWeight + LiquidityWeight + SpreadWeight = 1.0
```

## Equivalence Detection Flow

```
Input: []Market from Kalshi + []Market from Polymarket
         ↓
Step 1: Heuristic matching
  - Normalize titles
  - Extract entities
  - Compare resolution dates
  - Calculate confidence score
         ↓
Step 2: Confidence check
  - Score >= 0.80 → Mark as match, done, log "heuristic"
  - Score < 0.80  → Proceed to AI layer
         ↓
Step 3: AI Tool Execution (parallel where possible)
  - check_opposites
  - check_synonyms
  - check_entity_match
  - check_date_alignment
  - check_structural_equivalence
         ↓
Step 4: Claude synthesis
  - Send tool results + market titles to Claude
  - Claude returns is_equivalent, are_opposites, confidence, reasoning
         ↓
Step 5: Return MatchResult
  - Method = "heuristic+ai"
  - Log full decision trail
```

## Routing Engine Flow

```
Input: MatchResult (equivalent markets from two venues)
       + OrderSide ("yes" or "no")
       + OrderSize ($ amount)
         ↓
Step 1: Staleness check
  - Flag markets with FetchedAt > 2 minutes ago
         ↓
Step 2: Score each venue
  - PriceScore: normalize prices across venues (higher = better)
  - SpreadScore: normalize spreads (lower spread = higher score)
  - LiquidityScore: normalize liquidity (higher = better)
  - TotalScore: weighted sum
         ↓
Step 3: Decision
  - Higher TotalScore wins
  - If within 5% → tie, add warning, default to higher liquidity
         ↓
Step 4: Build RoutingDecision
  - RecommendedVenue
  - All VenueScores
  - Human-readable Reasoning
  - Any Warnings
```

## HTTP Server Endpoints

```
GET  /search?q={query}           → returns []MatchResult (matched market pairs)
POST /route                      → accepts {market_id, side, size} → RoutingDecision
GET  /health                     → returns {"status": "ok"}
GET  /                           → serves embedded index.html
```

## Embedded Static Files
The HTML UI is embedded in the binary at compile time.

```go
//go:embed static/index.html
var staticFiles embed.FS
```

## Configuration — All From Environment
```go
// config/config.go
type Config struct {
    AnthropicAPIKey             string
    KalshiBaseURL               string        // default: https://trading-api.kalshi.com/trade-api/v2
    PolymarketBaseURL           string        // default: https://gamma-api.polymarket.com
    HTTPTimeout                 time.Duration // default: 10s
    ServerPort                  string        // default: 8080
    HeuristicConfidenceThreshold float64      // default: 0.80
    PriceDataStalenessThreshold  time.Duration // default: 2m
}
```
